--!strict

-- Inventory manifests for imported assets.
--
-- Generated by scripts/generate-asset-certification.studio.luau. Regenerate an
-- entry rather than hand-editing it: the whole value of this file is that it
-- reflects exactly what an asset contained when it was accepted.
--
-- Why this file exists, and what it is actually for
-- -------------------------------------------------
-- Practically every system in this game is imported, and imported content is
-- full of scripts. A single vehicle carries between seventeen and forty-five
-- executables across its chassis, lighting kit and sound system, and it cannot
-- drive without them. A rule that forbids scripts outright would therefore be
-- bypassed on every asset, which protects nothing and blocks everything.
--
-- What a manifest buys instead is change detection. It pins the exact set of
-- executables present at the moment the asset was accepted, so anything that
-- appears afterwards -- a backdoor added to a model, a script introduced by a
-- marketplace update, an edit nobody meant to publish -- fails validation and
-- names itself, rather than running unnoticed on the live server.
--
-- It is deliberately NOT a claim that anybody has read these scripts. The
-- ReviewedBy line on each entry says so plainly, and it must stay honest: this
-- is provenance and tamper-detection, not a source audit. Treat an unexpected
-- validation failure here as a real question about the asset, not as noise to
-- be silenced by regenerating the manifest without looking.
--
-- Adding a new import
-- -------------------
--   1. Install the asset under ServerStorage.RoleplayOSAssets at its AssetPath.
--   2. Point TARGET_PATH/ASSET_ID in the generator at it and run it in Studio.
--   3. Paste the printed block below, then correct Source to say where it
--      genuinely came from.
--   4. Re-run the place and confirm the asset stops reporting UNSAFE_*.

local IMPORTED_KIT_REVIEW = "Imported asset inventory pinned by "
	.. "generate-asset-certification.studio.luau; not a line-by-line source review"

return {
